    deontological: A0 [PROVISIONAL_LEANING]
      Question: What additional framework-specific ground would resolve this validation result: A0 ADJUDICATION_CALIBRATION: perfect positive duty lacks a right-correlative, undertaking, or grounded emergency basis
      Answer: Ground: Kantian perfect positive rescue duty applies when (1) a moral agent uniquely controls an
              indispensible means to prevent imminent serious bodily harm or death to others, (2) doing so imposes
              only moderate self-cost (here, the opportunity cost of future food), and (3) the threatened parties
              retain their capacity for ends. These conditions create a right-correlative claim of urgent
              assistance for the endangered persons even absent a special relationship. Hence A0 satisfies that
              perfect duty; A1 violates its correlative right by withholding the only available lifesaving
              resource.
      Outcome: RESOLVED; current=NO_CHANGE; boundary=NOT_APPLICABLE; verification=VERIFIED_RESOLVED
